1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,480
And now it's the old scout master.

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:12,040
Well, listen, if you go up to Canada and you go to all that trouble, you'll want to see

3
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:13,840
a moose.

4
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:16,040
That's where we were last week canoeing

5
00:00:16,040 --> 00:00:18,360
Two crews from our troop.

6
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:24,520
One crew- one of the adults was a very experienced guy and had been up there several times, and

7
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:26,480
so he was being the advisor for that crew.

8
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:28,680
I was being the advisor for the other crew

9
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:33,880
And in my crew I had one adult who had been up there two or three times and I had one adult

10
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:37,680
who this was his first time up, so he was anxious to see a moose.

11
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:40,320
So we got together with the other crew at one point during the trip.

12
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:43,960
They were camped on the same lake but a distance away,

13
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:47,560
And the adult from that crew told the story of getting up in the morning, going retrieving

14
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:53,240
the bear bag and having two moose just kind of step right up to him,

15
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:56,800
You know, just dangerously close.

16
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:58,320
He did not feel comfortable,

17
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:00,480
But he got to see these two moose

18
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:05,239
And the one fellow that was with me was a little jealous, you know, because he'd been looking

19
00:01:05,239 --> 00:01:09,560
for moose and the other guy, you know, they just kind of showed up.

20
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:14,600
So a couple of days passed and then we heard another story where the guys were sitting

21
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:17,000
in their campsite. in the other crew, right

22
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,039
Moose comes right up out of the lake, you know, swam across the lake, comes right

23
00:01:21,039 --> 00:01:25,080
up, walks right through the campsite, doesn't seem to pay them any mind or anything like

24
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:26,080
that.

25
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:27,760
So they got to see this other moose

26
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:30,560
And the guy with me is starting to get a little chaffed.

27
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:33,560
You know why can't I find a moose.

28
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:34,560
So this is what we figured.

29
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:39,480
The moose all got together last week, you know, and they said: listen, there's these

30
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:43,880
two crews coming up and there's one guy in the crew. you know, he's kind of medium,

31
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:50,000
billed, dark hair, medium height, wears a tan shirt and green pants,

32
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,680
And don't go near that guy,

33
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:54,160
Don't go near him, you know.

34
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:59,560
But the other adults with that, with those two crews, you know, just to kind of mess

35
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:04,520
with that guy, just walk right up next to him.

36
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:07,000
I mean, at least that's what seemed to have happened.

37
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,440
But I've got to tell you the other fella, his name is Bill,

38
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:14,000
He got to see his moose before we left and he was a happy guy.

39
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,359
So you know, if you're going to go up to Canada, make sure to keep your eyes

40
00:02:18,359 --> 00:02:19,359
open.

41
00:02:19,359 --> 00:02:21,359
Moose might just scroll right into your campsite,

42
00:02:21,359 --> 00:02:22,359
You never know.

